# GitHub Client Delivery Token Flow

## Objective

Allow GitHub Actions in our source repository to automatically push files/builds into a client's GitHub repository.

---

# Architecture Overview

Source Repository
↓
GitHub Actions
↓
Client Repository Token
↓
Client Repository
↓
Delivery Report

Example:

Source Repository:
raconsys-governance-lab/project-demo

Client Repository:
Amit96-dev/client-repo-test

---

# Step 1 - Client Creates Repository

The client creates a repository that will receive releases/builds.

Example:

Amit96-dev/client-repo-test

Future examples:

client-company/frontend-release

client-company/backend-release

client-company/production-builds

This repository is owned by the client.

---

# Step 2 - Client Generates Access Token

Login to Client GitHub Account.

Navigate:

Profile Picture
→ Settings
→ Developer Settings
→ Personal Access Tokens
→ Fine-grained Tokens
→ Generate New Token

---

# Step 3 - Configure Token

Token Name:

Client Delivery Token

or

Project Sync Token

---

Repository Access:

Only selected repositories

Select:

client-repo-test

---

Repository Permissions:

Contents → Read and Write

No other permissions required for basic delivery.

---

# Step 4 - Generate Token

Click:

Generate Token

GitHub provides a token.

Example:

github_pat_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

Important:

Copy immediately.

GitHub will not display it again.

---

# Step 5 - Store Token In Source Repository

Login to Source Repository Account.

Repository:

raconsys-governance-lab/project-demo

Navigate:

Settings
→ Secrets and Variables
→ Actions
→ New Repository Secret

---

Secret Name:

CLIENT_REPO_TOKEN

Secret Value:

github_pat_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

Save Secret.

---

# Step 6 - Configure Workflow

Inside GitHub Action:

env:
CLIENT_REPO: Amit96-dev/client-repo-test

This defines the target repository.

---

# Step 7 - GitHub Action Uses Token

Example:

git clone [https://x-access-token:${{](https://x-access-token:${{) secrets.CLIENT_REPO_TOKEN }}@github.com/${CLIENT_REPO}.git

What happens:

GitHub Actions reads the token.

GitHub authenticates.

GitHub allows access to the client repository.

Client repository is cloned.

---

# Step 8 - Sync Files

Example:

cp README.md client-repo/

Future examples:

cp build.zip client-repo/

cp app.jar client-repo/

cp frontend-build/* client-repo/

Files are copied into the client repository.

---

# Step 9 - Commit Changes

GitHub Actions creates a commit:

git add .
git commit -m "Sync from project-demo"

This creates a delivery commit inside the client repository.

---

# Step 10 - Push To Client Repository

GitHub Actions executes:

git push

Result:

Files appear automatically inside the client repository.

No manual work required.

---

# Step 11 - Generate Delivery Report

GitHub Actions creates:

delivery-report.txt

Example:

CLIENT DELIVERY REPORT

Source Repository:
raconsys-governance-lab/project-demo

Target Repository:
Amit96-dev/client-repo-test

Triggered By:
